      "writtenOn": "2023-02-10T09:17:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not convinced this comment is true, except for the in-process case.\nTwo processes never share the same fds; they may have fds to the same file, but that\u0027s different.\nBut perhaps we should dup as part of parceling for the in-process case.\nDo we need a close on VMD? Otherwise, how do the fds ever get closed?\n\nOr should we close on writeToParcel (via PARCELABLE_WRITE_RETURN_VALUE)? But then calling write twice needs to become an error.",
